$ DNFB_11_paper_aligned: conservative paper-aligned variant of DNFB_11.
$ Added from Dai et al. (Materials 2022, 15, 7648), Table 1:
$   L0(LIQUID,Nd,Dy)=700 J/mol; L0(BCC_A2,Nd,Dy)=680 J/mol.
$ Added an HCP_A3 Nd-Dy solution with L0=-1550+0.61*T J/mol,
$ using the available unary functions as an engineering approximation.
$ Extended FE4NDB4 (tau2=RE1.1Fe4B4) to an Nd/Dy rare-earth sublattice
$ and added the Dai Table 1 Dy endmember. The separate DYFE4B4 phase
$ is omitted in this variant to avoid double-counting tau2.
$ The original DNFB_11.tdb remains unchanged.
$------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ DNFB_11 = DNFB_9b_clean with T1-Dy magnetism set to Yang 2025 (TC 594.1, BMAGN 0.59). No other change.
$------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ DNFB_9b_clean.tdb = DNFB_9_ternliq.tdb with comment-only edits. No parameter changed.
$ Project: Nd-Dy-Fe-B TDB for ThermoLM. Stage: Dy-Fe-B checked against Yang 2025.
$ Tolerance: 30 K on liquidus and invariant temperatures. Phase-set near-ties under about
$ 300 J/atom are logged as known misses.
$ STATUS, Fe-rich Dy-Fe-B, solid state 1000-1200 K: 6 of 8 scoreable Yang alloys pass
$ (A3 A7 B1 B2 B9 B10). Known misses: A1, A2 (T1 beats DyFe4B4 by 21 and 253 J/atom).
$ Unscoreable with line compounds: A4 A5 A8 B3 B11. A6 skipped.
$ Alloy scoring was last run on DNFB_8 and has NOT been rerun with the ternary liquid term.
$ LIQUID: E1 and E2 first liquid about 1357 K against Yang 1381 K (about 25 K low).
$ NOT VALIDATED: Dy-rich and B-rich corners, any Nd-containing composition.
$ NOT PRESENT: tau4 Dy5Fe2B4, tau5 Dy3FeB7, tau6 DyFeB4, Dy2B, HCP_A3.
$ Fe-B source differs from Yang: Hallstedt (94Hal1) here, Witusiewicz 2019 there.
$------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ BFEND
$
